    <body>
      <div type="work" n="235">
        <pb n="278"/>
        <head>The first on the Resurrection.</head>
        <div type="preface">
          <ab n="1">Again Other Short Oblational Hymns That Are Sung after the Reception of the Mysteries : and They Are Those That Are Sung in the Churches of the Cities, Having Been Drawn up by Certain Ancient Industrious Men and Poets (<foreign xml:lang="grc">ποιηταί</foreign>).</ab>
        </div>
        <div type="section">
          <ab n="2">235 — i. — In keeping the feast of thy Resurrection from among the dead, <persName>Christ</persName>, God, we have been filled<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a1" target="#n1" n="1"/> with joy and spiritual gladness, Halleluyah!</ab>
        </div>
      </div>
      <noteGrp>
        <note xml:id="n1" target="#a1" n="1"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 278, n. 1</orig></choice> Ps. cxxxv, 1 (not quoted).</note>
